   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Lance Corporal Aaron M. Swanson Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S6528",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6528-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-i, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6528\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Lance Corporal Aaron M. Swanson Memori-\nal Highway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDesignates State Route 394 in the Village of Lakewood, County of Chau-\ntauqua, as the \"Lance Corporal Aaron M. Swanson Memorial Highway.\"\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law by adding a new section 344-h, which\ndesignates State Route 394 in the Village of Lakewood, county of Chau-\ntauqua, as the \"Lance Corporal Aaron M. Swanson Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection 2: States that the commissioner of transportation shall provide\nfor the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the state\nhighway systems as designated pursuant to section 1 of this act. The\ndesignation will be for ceremonial purposes only, and the roads official\nname will not be changed as a result of this act.\n\nSection 3: Provides that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLance Corporal Aaron M. Swanson served his nation in Afghanistan\nassigned to the United States Marine's 3rd Battalion, 25th Marine Regi-\nment, 4th Marine Division, Marine Forces Reserve, Buffalo, New York.\nLance Corporal Swanson tragically lost his life in service to our coun-\ntry on February 7, 2011 while conducting combat operations in Garmsir\nDistrict, Helmand Province, Afghanistan.\n\nLance Corporal Swanson was a native of Lakewood, New York, a graduate of\nSouthwestern High School in Jamestown, and attended Jamestown Community\nCollege prior to serving in the Marines. The Chautauqua County Legisla-\nture has expressed its desire to honor Lance Corporal Swanson. The Chau-\ntauqua County Legislature, by unanimous vote, adopted a formal resol-\nution requesting this legislation. The dedication of State Route 394 in\nthe Village of Lakewood is but one small way for this state to honor the\nbravery, dedication and ultimate sacrifice of this brave American hero.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018: S.8854/A.10973 Passed Senate\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
